 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send everything that lands in someone's notification tray to their phone and desktop as a push notification.
+Push notifications are signed with a VAPID key pair, which you can generate with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails push:keys
+```
+
+That prints a pair of values that you then pass to the container:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+Keep the same pair for the lifetime of your instance: changing it invalidates every subscription people have already made.
+If you don't set these, push notifications are turned off and Fizzy won't offer them in notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
